Pinned mise configuration and scripts/openspec-setup.mbtx are adapted from
moonrockz/diagrams.mbt, revision 79ae56e2bdaf77ad5ed6951c8e2d856b3fffb38a,
under Apache-2.0. Changes include Telescope names and setup-only tasks.

The documentation template assets are copied with a responsive wrapping change
to agent-document.css and a comment clarification in the HTML templates;
vendored highlight assets are unchanged. The adapted schema
replaces Morphir's shared tracker rules with Telescope's repository-local policy.
Vendored highlight.js 11.12.0 keeps its BSD 3-Clause license and upstream record
in docs/templates/assets/highlight/LICENSE and UPSTREAM.md.

The reusable site library in pkgs/telescope/model, content, markdown, site,
views, islands and assets is adapted from moonrockz/diagrams.mbt apps/site,
revision 79ae56e2bdaf77ad5ed6951c8e2d856b3fffb38a, under Apache-2.0.
This includes the embedded notebooks moon-doc package and module-index fixtures
in model/api_fixture_test.mbt, recorded with MoonBit 0.10.17+093cb8f9c.
Changes separate portable content analysis from native CommonMark rendering,
remove diagram engines, generalize consumer configuration and branding,
exclude development artifacts, add explicit provider hooks and output validation,
and preserve API and version navigation contracts.

Smithy and Morphir site engine files remain read-only references. Smithy's site
records its moonspec ancestor moonrockz/moonspec revision
9ea9a688c3a39d95c91a28b2a40bb5332e8786f5; no Smithy domain code is included.

The native host in pkgs/telescope/host adapts diagrams.mbt's apps/site/generate,
apps/site/check, apps/site/assemble and scripts/serve-site.mbtx from the
Apache-2.0 source baseline documented above. Subsequent provider-anchor behavior
also follows diagrams.mbt commit e0a541033c77590d4c51ecfeb7fb2932e5c478c4.

The default shell palette in pkgs/telescope/assets/site.css is adapted from
moonrockz/smithy site/public/styles.css, revision
b97203cea93ed2b71affc1580817ecfd41a6b515, under Apache-2.0.
Changes map indigo and cool-neutral tokens to Telescope's existing variable
names, distinguish essential control boundaries, and retain semantic statuses.
No Smithy domain engine, branding or gallery runtime is included.

The general editor and tutorial packages are original Telescope implementations
of the approved shared contracts. Smithy behavior and lexical scanning were
reviewed as source references at revision
caa78a677b88fdf506eb77953453d2519f1f4786, with codec compatibility decisions
from e3c140d11dba72b5f642c1e634bd94ec4adc2c94. No Smithy engine or lesson
corpus is included. See pkgs/telescope/editor/browser/UPSTREAM.md and the
OpenSpec design source inventory for selected files and ownership.

The tutorial TOML boundary uses moonbit-community/toml@0.5.0, Apache-2.0,
without copying the parser implementation. Optional CodeMirror/Lezer editor
bundles retain pinned MIT dependency notices in
pkgs/telescope/editor/browser/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt; native CLI archives
and generated editor assets include that file.
